Methods the JDK has and TeaVM's classlib lacks at 9be5eca57, needed by Minecraft 26.2's server (mctick) and its libraries,
and class-path resources for the low-level targets (served from the virtual file system under /res/: TeaVM's own
resource support is JavaScript-only). UUID is replaced by the JDK's two-long layout (TeaVM's held a String: no
(long, long) constructor and string-compare equality, which would have taxed every UUID-keyed map on the tick).
New classes these methods return (FileChannel, FileStore, ...) are in wjharness/bench/teavm-classlib, which
teavm-cli.sh compiles into the same classlib module.
Codegen: adds methods and one class rewrite (UUID); a program that reaches none of them compiles as before.

